WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
A spaceship explodes.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:06.010
In the films, you hear
a huge, rumbling boom.

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.870
But in real space, watching
from another ship,

4
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.550
you would see the flash
and hear nothing at all.

5
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.870
Total silence.

6
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.950
So what stops the sound?

7
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.130
First, you'll find out what
a wave really carries,

8
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.410
starting with ripples on a pond.

9
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:25.490
Then you'll see how a vibration
makes a sound, why sounds echo,

10
00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.370
and how your ear drum and
a microphone pick them up.

11
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.770
Is space just too cold for sound?

12
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.850
Your mission: explain why a
space battle would be silent.
